you have to be incredibly fit these  actors put in some serious work at the  gym transforming into a superhero is  easier said than done find out the  extreme diets and workout regimens it  takes to be a hero in the mcu training  for  about six or eight months for that first  film it takes a lot of hard work for  chris hemsworth to maintain the god of  thunder's impressive physique the  workouts he does include working on his  core kickboxing and even surfing one of  hemsworth's favorite hobbies his trainer  luke zaki stated that the majority of  the work they do is done months before  the movies to ensure hemsworth is camera  ready chris is so strong that when zaki  holds the pads for hemsworth to kick he  has to brace himself because chris is  powerful enough to knock him down like  i'd rather sort of feel good and look  that extra bit you know when kumail  nanjiani was cast as kingo in the  eternals fans wondered how the comedian  would translate to a superhero role he  answered with a shirtless picture on  instagram that showed off his new  physique this impressive transformation  was a result of a full year of work  nanjiani stated his strict diet was the  hardest part as he didn't eat any  refined sugar and almost no carbs for a  year the hard work clearly paid off  though as his new look even garnered  praise from dwayne johnson he said uh  dense muscle is hard to achieve my  brother he thinks my muscle is dense  before guardians of the galaxy pratt was  known as the schlubby comedian on parks  and rec but quickly proved he was much  more pratt lost 60 pounds in six months  working three or four hours a day of  just consistent ass kicking hard work  trainer duffy gaver had nothing but  praise for pratt's work ethic and  commitment he isn't the client you have  to push he's the type of client you have  to pull down with guardians of the  galaxy 3 coming up next we're sure pratt  will be hard at work again the secret is  you can't do it  in a month robert downey jr has been  training with wing chun a technique made  famous by bruce lee since 2003. when it  came time to play tony stark downey kept  this in his regimen as well as adding  kung fu qigong and strength training his  trainer brad bose made it his focus to  increase downey's muscle we cut way back  on cardio and really increased the  weight he was lifting down he was able  to add on 25 pounds of muscle after  months of work and consuming 5 000  calories a day five years ago what used  to be my get in shape plan is moot and  useless renner had some experience with  getting in shape before his turn as  clint barton in the mcu and carried over  that work ethic to get in shape for  hawkeye he posted himself lifting some  weights in preparation for his role in  the disney plus series hawkeye in terms  of sharpening his archery skills renner  has actually trained with olympic  archers for the films but it apparently  isn't as helpful as you might think um  got pretty good at it actually but it  doesn't really serve me too for for  hawkeye stuff evans put in a ton of work  to attain his super soldier body for the  first movie evans went to the gym four  to five days a week for three months  training for about two hours a day  working with trainer simon waterson  evans was able to get his body fat down  to eight percent while working on civil  war the hardest part for evans was the  amount of food he had to consume as well  as the kind of food just bland naked  pieces of chicken and rice and it's it's  it's not that appetizing  when johansson got the role of black  widow she admitted that she had never  stepped foot in a gym before that  quickly changed however johansen and her  trainer eric johnson agreed to focus on  strength and functional movements not  looks it took about a year to reach her  desired fitness goals and she has kept  it up for all her marvel movies i am  stronger and more capable now than i was  10 years ago which is so awesome to be  able to say fit in my everyday life i  like to feel strong it's part of my  mental well-being the late chadwick  boseman already had a martial arts  background when he was cast as the black  panther his trainer addison henderson  focused on non-stop training that had  bozeman constantly moving working out up  to four hours a day it was an intense  experience for bozeman fight training  conditioning eating a certain amount it  was hardcore basically it was like  training like a fighter you know tom  holland was one of the most athletic and  fit actors coming into his mcu role  bringing with him a background in  gymnastics and dancing for spider-man  holland started boxing and going to the  gym every morning for about an hour with  his trainer i look up i look up to  boxers a lot he also did ems training  where he wore a suit with pads that  would send electrical shocks through his  muscles it's a lot of fun and it works  but it really is the worst thing i've  ever done sebastian stan admitted that  at the time of getting the role he  didn't know his body well or whether his  diet was good or not it was the first  thing he and his trainer addressed as  they figured out what routine and diet  was best for him stan was often in the  gym starting every session with a heavy  lift he discussed the effects his  workouts have on him it's gonna motivate  you to be more  driven in the other aspects of your life  brie larson was the first female  superhero to lead her own movie in the  mcu so she wanted to prove that she  belonged right alongside the rest of the  avengers she did 9 months of training in  total sometimes doing her sessions five  times a week her trainer jason walsh  praised her effort she did the work  nutrition recovery sleep everything  required of her larsen can now do some  seriously impressive feats of strength  including a one-armed pull-up and  pushing a 5 000 pound jeep it's been a  really powerful journey for me to learn  what my body can do paul rudd is much  like chris pratt in that when he joined  the mcu he was known for being a  not-too-fit comedic actor that all  changed when he got in shape for his  role as ant-man rudd was motivated to  get in shape as he wanted to get into  the mindset of his character and really  fit the part i figured if i'm in really  good shape i will feel like less of an  imposter in the role the hard work paid  off but rudd said it meant not doing  anything fun for a year basically made  health and fitness the focus of my day  to prepare for her role as mantis palm  clementiev didn't take the traditional  route her co-stars did to get in shape  all her work was practical consisting of  stunt and fight training in one video  she can be seen doing sit-ups while  hanging off of a punching bag  maintaining a healthy diet is a  difficulty for clementiev when she tries  to cut something out she becomes  obsessed with it for me it's about  quantity balance i eat a little bit of  everything when i had that the addition  had no idea how big the character would  be lily got in great shape for the  ant-man movies but revealed that she  suffers from chronic back pain she  stated she spent a good portion of the  last two years in bed as she had a  physical breakdown fortunately she seems  to be taking control of her body now as  she is focusing on foundation training  to rebuild her base she even posted a  picture of herself on twitter with the  caption  wasp ready arms signaling she is  prepared to portray the wasp again i was  asking to build a lot of these s curves  into her fight style cumberbatch did all  the traditional working out and dieting  to prepare for doctor strange you spend  months eating the right stuff doing the  right kind of press ups and pull-ups and  dips and all the other jazz he revealed  a strange technique he was taught to  look his best on camera it involved  dehydrating himself the night before and  then the day of shooting eating a rather  odd combination of foods you basically  are told to eat skittles and drink  coffee because it dehydrates you so  basically your skin then shrink wraps  around the muscle fiber we have nothing  but respect for the hard work and  dedication these actors put towards  getting into shape for their roles  maintaining a superhero physique is no  easy task but these actors were up to  the challenge which transformation did  you find most impressive

